    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="089e9e31-6c28-5466-a25f-bb7b07fd7df9" activityNameId="e61ad715-c3d3-5173-a789-26dcfdb54c9e" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">xx Copper, primary, at refinery</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: xx Copper, primary, at refinery
The product "copper, primary, at refinery" is used as pure metal or as alloying element in various technical applications.;
CAS number: 007440-50-8; 
UUID: f5faeb9a-32cd-3d24-946f-5e9274ad5a8f
The module includes the pre-treatment of the ore, the reduction and the refining copper to cathode copper, including the country-specific share in hydrometalurgically won copper (SX-EW)
Location: This module is valid for the whole corresponding region. Some agents used like lime or sodium cyanide originate from data sets valid for Switzerland or Europe.
Technology: The ore is pre-treated,  reduced and refined according to the country specific mix of process alternatives: reverberatory furnace 23.3%; flash smelting furnaces 53.9%; other 5.2%.; SX-EW 17.6%. An overall abatement for sulphur dioxide of 50.0% was estimated.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: 9.5 million tonnes in Cu in 1994
Sampling: literature 
Extrapolations: see Geography and Technology
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_f5faeb9a-32cd-3d24-946f-5e9274ad5a8f.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="9aaa4753-f7ef-5e0d-bcb0-bc5f01164c5b" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
